## Interface: 100007, 16001
## Title: |cff888888Spoken Player (now Spoken)|r
## Notes: Spoken Player is now Spoken. This folder never loads and is safe to delete.
## Version: 3.2.0
## Group: Spoken
## LoadOnDemand: 1
# A tombstone, with no Lua. Spoken Player became Spoken in 3.0.0, and unzipping a release adds
# the Spoken folder without removing SpokenPlayer: the old player went on loading beside the
# new one, narrating over it and failing to register the minimap button Spoken already holds.
# The packagers write this file over every .toc name the old folder ever had, each with its
# client's Interface line (scripts/lib/tombstone.sh), so an unzip leaves the old folder with
# nothing to load. LoadOnDemand keeps the client from loading even the empty addon, which is
# also what keeps Spoken's leftover-folder warning quiet.
